    "outputs": {
      "DIFFICULTY_EXPLANATION": "The task couples ten differentiated Linux resource families through shared Terraform lifecycle semantics: stable external identity, native drift observation, transactional mutation/state publication, scoped ownership, runner failure behavior and canonical normalization. Correctness therefore depends on coherent cross-component invariants rather than isolated resource CRUD.",
      "README_PATH": "terraform-ansible-managed-resources/README.md",
      "SOLUTION_EXPLANATION": "The reference completion centralizes lifecycle identity/normalization and uses structured Ansible execution for Create/Update/Delete while Read observes Linux state natively. State advances only after successful mutation; failures remain retryable, owned deletions remain scoped, and equivalent representations converge without replay.",
      "VERIFICATION_EXPLANATION": "Structural verification maps the public contract to 30 F2P and 6 P2P cases, with same-chat Q1 NO_GAP, Q2 COVERED and Q3 CLEAR. Fresh empirical Oracle/NOP execution remains intentionally deferred to the registered DETERMINISTIC_VALIDATION gate and is not claimed here."
    },
